==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*3 [[Lophiiformes Angaburu]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 76.67 seconds<sup>2,300f</sup>.
*1 [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] spawns as the boss after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*2 [[Suidae Piggicus|Suidae Piggici]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 70 seconds<sup>2,100f</sup>.
*4 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 140 seconds<sup>4,200f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Pigge]] spawns once 20 Cat Units have been defeated.
*2 [[Pigge]]s spawn once 50 Cat Units have been defeated, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Pigge]]s spawn once 120 Cat Units have been defeated, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn once 200 Cat Units have been defeated, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is very tight on money, so a Rich Cat can help a ton if you're struggling in that aspect. A great approach here is to primarily bring [[Behemoth Slayer]] Cats. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]], and especially [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] work best here. Naala is an excellent choice due to their low standing range and Immunity to Surges. Additionally, [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] help deal with incoming Brollows and the Lophiiformes Angaburu.

